# Apple ld(1) -exported_symbols_list — counterpart of
# cmake/librescrs-public-exports.map (GNU ld --version-script).
#
# Whitelists LM-public C++ symbols by mangled-name prefix:
#   * `__ZN9LibreSCRS*` — every `LibreSCRS::*` namespace member
#                         (the leading `_` is Apple's convention; the
#                         Itanium-ABI mangling on Darwin is `_ZN9...` with
#                         the extra `_` prefix making it `__ZN9...`).
#                         Covers the LM-internal cross-`.so` ABI shared
#                         with card plugins via the
#                         `LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::` namespace.
#
# Everything else (bundled OpenSSL, libresign internals, vendored
# nlohmann / miniz / pugixml) collapses to hidden so the public macOS
# ABI is the LibreSCRS namespace only — no symbol bleed-through from
# statically linked third-party archives, no accidental coupling to
# internal LibreSCRS namespaces that happen to live outside
# `LibreSCRS::*`.
#
# Linux parity note: cmake/librescrs-public-exports.map (the GNU ld
# version-script counterpart) matches the same mangled-prefix families,
# each anchored on `9LibreSCRS` right after its prefix. The vtable and
# typeinfo entries carry the nested-name `N` before the anchor for the
# same reason as there: `__ZTV*LibreSCRS*` also admitted the vtable of
# a standard-library template instantiated on a LibreSCRS type, such as
# `std::_Sp_counted_ptr_inplace<LibreSCRS::Trust::TrustStore, ...>`.
# Both modes preserve the same intentional cross-`.so`
# `LibreSCRS::*::Internal::` reach surface via the `__ZN9LibreSCRS*`
# prefix family below.

__ZN9LibreSCRS*
__ZNK9LibreSCRS*
__ZNO9LibreSCRS*
__ZTVN9LibreSCRS*
__ZTIN9LibreSCRS*
__ZTSN9LibreSCRS*
